# RGJ-RC1-011B — pinned graphics/input/lifecycle consolidation contract
# Upstream pin: TASEmulators/freej2me-plus@13ec186903087156c145268f8706eecfaf9f1e50
# This supersedes only unsafe/inexact portions of patches 0010/0012/0013.
# It is not BUILD-PASS.

OWNERSHIP
- PlatformImage remains image decode/facade owner; RG35XXImageCache remains the only RG35XX immutable decode cache.
- PlatformGraphics remains all MIDP/DoJa drawing owner; RG35XXTransformCache remains geometry-only transform cache.
- MobilePlatform remains front/backbuffer, flush, resize and FPS-limit owner.
- Libretro remains the 5-byte stdin protocol and stdout video serializer owner.
- RG35XXInputEngine remains the only RG35XX held/repeat state machine.
- RG35XXLifecycle remains the only RG35XX subsystem-order coordinator.
- No second renderer, frame thread, protocol reader, key mapper, or lifecycle owner is added.

A. PLATFORMIMAGE / PLATFORMGRAPHICS
Apply existing 0011 cache integration and 0007/0008 graphics contracts against the pinned blobs. Do not replace the classes. Immutable byte-array image cache hits reconstruct a fresh TYPE_INT_ARGB image. Mutable DoJa byte-array images bypass cache. processAlpha=false still forces opaque pixels; it is not a raw alpha-preserving arraycopy.

B. MOBILEPLATFORM EXACT DIRTY PRODUCER POINTS
Pinned `MobilePlatform.flushGraphics()` performs:
  synchronized(lcdFrontbuffer) { gcFrontbuffer.flushGraphics(...); }
  if(postDraw != null) { postDraw.run(); postDraw = null; }
  painter.run();
  ...
  limitFps();

If dirty generation is maintained, call `RG35XXFrameScheduler.markDirty()` only after `postDraw` has completed and before `painter.run()`. This represents the final visible frontbuffer state for that flush. Do not mark per primitive.

Pinned `resizeLCD()` replaces lcdFrontbuffer/lcd and graphics/display references. Mark dirty only after all replacement references are installed.

IMPORTANT RC1 REPLACEMENT OF PATCH 0012 CONSUMER RULE:
Do NOT call `RG35XXFrameScheduler.waitForChange()` from Libretro case 15 or anywhere in the single `LibretroIO` protocol-reader thread. That thread blocks in `System.in.read()` and owns all control parsing; a dirty wait there can prevent future core packets from being consumed. The current case-15 protocol also expects a frame response when requested and has no explicit no-change packet. Therefore RC1 retains the existing frame request/response transport. Dirty generation remains producer/lifecycle state until a non-blocking no-change protocol or independently proven presentation worker exists. Do not add a second Java frame thread solely to consume the scheduler.

C. LIBRETRO INPUT EXACT CALL SITES
Create one reusable static/final `RG35XXInputEngine.Sink` in Libretro:
  keyPressed(slot)  -> MobilePlatform.keyPressed(Mobile.getMobileKey(slot))
  keyReleased(slot) -> MobilePlatform.keyReleased(Mobile.getMobileKey(slot))
  keyRepeated(slot) -> MobilePlatform.keyRepeated(Mobile.getMobileKey(slot))

Valid RG35XX joypad slots are 0..19. `MobilePlatform.pressedKeys` is length 23 in the pin; index 20 is upstream fast-forward state and must not be passed to RG35XXInputEngine. Preserve indexes 20+ for their existing non-key semantics.

case 3 DOWN:
- if code outside 0..19, ignore as a joypad transition;
- set pressedKeys[code]=true;
- call RG35XXInputEngine.press(code, System.currentTimeMillis(), sink);
- do not call MobilePlatform.keyPressed separately.

case 2 UP:
- same slot validation;
- set pressedKeys[code]=false;
- call RG35XXInputEngine.release(code, sink);
- do not call MobilePlatform.keyReleased separately.

case 15:
- replace the pinned loop that directly calls keyRepeated for every pressedKeys entry with exactly one `RG35XXInputEngine.update(System.currentTimeMillis(), sink)`.
- preserve fast-forward index 20 handling and all pause/frame serialization behavior.
- if native media event drain from 0017 is present, drain it in the same bounded tick without introducing another thread.

D. LIFECYCLE LOAD TRANSACTION
Before `MobilePlatform.load(...)` in case 10:
  RG35XXLifecycle.beforeGameLoad();
This is mandatory before loader/suite context can be replaced.

If load succeeds:
  RG35XXLifecycle.afterGameLoad();
Then continue current restart/config/run flow.

If load fails or throws before success commit:
  RG35XXLifecycle.gameLoadFailed();
Do not fabricate gameActive=true.

The updated project `RG35XXLifecycle.beforeGameLoad()` now prepares/reset state but keeps gameActive=false; `afterGameLoad()` is the explicit success commit point.

E. PAUSE / SHUTDOWN
When the libretro facade initiates a MIDlet pause, execute the RMS pause barrier before volatile application state is considered safely paused. Final control-pipe EOF/shutdown behavior remains governed by 0017: call RG35XXLifecycle.platformShutdown() before Java exits where possible, with native hard-kill only as fallback after bounded shutdown ownership.

F. PRESERVE
- stdout remains video only.
- synchronized frontbuffer copy/serialization remains intact.
- Mobile.getMobileKey remains the single profile/numeric mapping owner.
- DoJa/Vodafone key-state behavior stays in MobilePlatform.
- existing `LockSupport` FPS limiter remains upstream-owned and is a build compatibility gate, not replaced here.

STATUS
STATIC-AUDIT-PASS is recorded only after the companion 011B audit checks this contract against the pinned source. BUILD-PASS and DEVICE-TEST-PASS remain separate.